\section{On "mission"}{

The BMF carries \strong{no mission statement} — that text lives on Form 990 Part I
/ Part III, not in the master file. The BMF's mission proxies, best to worst:
\itemize{
\item \code{ntee_code_definition} — the NTEE classification in words
("Cemeteries", "Elementary & Secondary Schools"). Always populated, but
~1 in 4 records reads \code{UNDEFINED}.
\item \code{nteev2_subsector} — the coarse sector (ART, EDU, HEL, HMS, REL ...).
Useful for a same-sector / different-sector test even when the detailed
code is undefined.
\item \code{activity_code_definitions} — legacy IRS activity codes rendered as
text ("Association or convention of churches; Other religious
activities"). Genuinely mission-like, but only ~44\% populated and frozen
in the 1970s vocabulary.
}
Where a real mission statement is available from an e-file extract it can be
joined on \code{ein} via \code{mission} — see \code{\link[=pf_attach_missions]{pf_attach_missions()}}.
}

